BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Moving Stories: Arts-based movement class for older adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T113000
UID:6a26cef0f56bd86e00b548a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Tiger princess dance projects\n\, a non-profit contemporary da
 nce company\, brings you a free custom designed arts-based movement class 
 for older adults. Join Artistic Director Yvonne Ng and her team of profess
 ional artists in a fun\, healthy\, and exciting arts program\,\nMoving Sto
 ries\n.\nThese free classes offer an introduction into the enriching world
  of art and creativity through movement and music. These activities have p
 roven to improve circulation\, retain joint mobility\, promote mental stim
 ulation\, improve posture and coordination\, and build strength and balanc
 e.\nNo previous movement experience required.\nSuggested Age: 60 +\nGo at 
 your own pace\, modifications encouraged\nExercises can be modified for se
 ated movement and/or standing
LOCATION:Leaside\, Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a26cef0f56bd86e00b548a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:North York Central Library Film Club - Special Movie Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260722T194500
UID:6a32e8d816554cd59fc978c7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please join us for an evening screening of "Black Bag".\nBlack
  Bag (2025)\nRunning time: 94 minutes\nDirector: Steven Soderbergh\nStarri
 ng: Cate Blanchett\, Michael Fassbender\, Marisa Abela\, Tom Burke\, Naomi
 e Harris\, Regé-Jean Page\, and Pierce Brosnan\nBlack Bag is a spy drama 
 about legendary intelligence agents George Woodhouse and his beloved wife 
 Kathryn. When she is suspected of betraying the nation\, George faces the 
 ultimate test of whether to be loyal to his marriage\, or to his country.\
 nThe North York Central Library Film Club meets monthly on Wednesdays. The
 re is a short\, informal discussion after the screening\, time permitting.
 \nRegistration is not required. Please contact the Browsery Department at 
 416-395-5672 for more information.\nNext dates:\nAugust 19 (Wednesday\, at
  2 PM): The Fantastic 4: First Steps
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32e8d816554cd59fc978c7
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Resilience in the Time We Are Living Now
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T143000
UID:69fe2ff0e8af4a2f007123b1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:​This presentation will discuss a clear definition of resili
 ence\, how to adapt and deal with life's challenges\, share the 4 phases o
 f resilience\, provide tips and tools to improve mental well-being and how
  to set goals that can be applied to challenging situations which will enh
 ance resiliency.\nParticipants can expect to gain an understanding of resi
 lience and how to apply it to their lives and challenges. We will discuss 
 the importance of identifying daily steps that will produce positive outco
 mes and begin to heal and grow new pathways with time and repetition.\nPre
 sented by retired City of Toronto social workers\, Jill Kumer and Bryna W
 asserman.
LOCATION:Barbara Frum\, Located in Room B on the third floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fe2ff0e8af4a2f007123b1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Vegetarian Sushi Making for Adults
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260804T153000
UID:69fb77cde8af4a2f00709b04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:TV host and celebrity chef Sang Kim will teach the basics of s
 ushi making. Participants will make sushi rolls using ingredients prepared
  by the Chef and eat their own creations. A brief history of sushi\, its o
 rigins and eating etiquette will also be shared.\nSpace is limited.\nTicke
 ts will be handed out 30 minutes prior to start time.
LOCATION:Runnymede\, 2nd Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69fb77cde8af4a2f00709b04
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
