BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Movies 
 Saturdays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T163000
UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d5a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nJuly 4th –\nThe Butler\nJul
 y 11th –\nNobody's Fool\nJuly 18th –\nNebraska\nJuly 25th –\nAll The
  Presidents Men\nDrop in\, no registration is required.\nSnacks and refres
 hments are provided for all participants. Ingredient lists will be availab
 le at the program.\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis
  Centre's F.R.E.S.H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d5a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
