BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Collage Social
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T153000
UID:6a3dc200c52cdc3600ecf1eb@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a friendly and fun hour and a half of collage. Cha
 t with other crafters to share your ideas and tips. All materials will be 
 provided and a selection of inspiring art books will be on display to get 
 your creative juices flowing.\nRegister here or call 416-396-8939 to regi
 ster.
LOCATION:Taylor Memorial\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3dc200c52cdc3600ecf1eb
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 3: PivotTables & Conditional Formatting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260719T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260719T153000
UID:6a1863eef56bd86e00b2bf07@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills and learn to use Ex
 cel data effectively.\nIn this third session\, you will:\nUse Conditional 
 Formatting to visualize data\nExplore the power of PivotTables for data su
 mmary and analysis\nSort and filter the data in tables and using slicers\n
 Take home practice data to improve your new skills\nUpon completion of thi
 s class\, you will be able to get more from your data using Pivot tables.\
 nPrerequisites:  Excel Basics 1 and 2 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse
  and keyboard skills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations\nInf
 ormation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is coll
 ected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, secti
 ons 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event
  and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how t
 he library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at
 \nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2
 G8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1863eef56bd86e00b2bf07
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ADULT BOARD GAME SOCIAL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260810T200000
UID:6a3983e8c78687f2fd2dde83@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us monthly at the Malvern Library for Adult Board Game So
 cial\, a relaxed evening of tabletop games and good company.\nHave a favou
 rite board game? Feel free to bring it along and share it with others. Sho
 rter and easy-to-learn games work best\, but there is always room to explo
 re something new together.\nThe library will also provide a selection of b
 oard games for casual play. No experience needed. This is a welcoming\, lo
 w-pressure space to learn\, play\, and connect with others.\nDrop-in.\nMon
 day\, July 13th 6-8pm\nMonday\, August 10th 6-8pm
LOCATION:Malvern\, 1st Floor Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3983e8c78687f2fd2dde83
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
