BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:ADULT BOARD GAME SOCIAL
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260713T200000
UID:6a3983e8c78687f2fd2dde82@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us monthly at the Malvern Library for Adult Board Game So
 cial\, a relaxed evening of tabletop games and good company.\nHave a favou
 rite board game? Feel free to bring it along and share it with others. Sho
 rter and easy-to-learn games work best\, but there is always room to explo
 re something new together.\nThe library will also provide a selection of b
 oard games for casual play. No experience needed. This is a welcoming\, lo
 w-pressure space to learn\, play\, and connect with others.\nDrop-in.\nMon
 day\, July 13th 6-8pm\nMonday\, August 10th 6-8pm
LOCATION:Malvern\, 1st Floor Community Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3983e8c78687f2fd2dde82
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ask a Sommelier: Navigating Wine Labels\, Lists\, and Restaurant E
 tiquette
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T200000
UID:6a47e7677e16a03d00e9fcd1@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to make smarter decisions as a consumer when buying wine
  in a store or in a restaurant. Sommelier Christopher Lafleur will make ap
 proaching a wine list (and the ritual around the first taste) make so much
  more sense by breaking down what is on labels\, teaching what terms are u
 seful\, and what terms don't mean anything.\nThis is an in-person program\
 , no registration required.
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a47e7677e16a03d00e9fcd1
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
