BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Golden Paintbrush-Painting for Seniors
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T133000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260723T150000
UID:6a39977190cc4e3a790ff3d4@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Embrace lifelong learning by trying a beginner-friendly acryli
 c painting class where no experience is necessary—just a willingness to 
 have fun and try something new. In this session\, you'll be guided step-by
 -step through a simple project by a supportive instructor. Learn the basic
 s of colour mixing\, brush techniques\, and composition\, while creating y
 our own beautiful artwork to take home. All materials—including paints\,
  brushes\, canvases\, and aprons—will be provided by the presenter. Just
  bring your creativity and a smile!
LOCATION:Humber Summit\, Humber Summit Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a39977190cc4e3a790ff3d4
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Apple Devices for Beginners
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260808T153000
UID:6a511c52fb418a28009a0510@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This class is for absolute beginners who are curious about buy
 ing an Apple iPhone or iPad\, or who have just acquired one and want to un
 derstand how it operates. In this beginner’s class you will learn about 
 the different parts of an Apple iPhone or iPad and where they are located\
 , what you need to make your iPhone or iPad run\, the Apple home screen\, 
 settings\, storage and troubleshooting.\nBring your own device: if you hav
 e an Apple device\, feel free to bring it with you and follow along with t
 he exercises.\nPlease register at tpl.ca or by calling 416-396-8943.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre (LC)\, 1st floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a511c52fb418a28009a0510
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Quilting Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260929T200000
UID:6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981bde@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:The focus of this program is to make quilts for donation\, usi
 ng fabrics that have been donated to the group for this purpose.\nParticip
 ants meet weekly to share ideas and inspiration while working on quilts. T
 here are no sewing machines at the library so any sewing is done by hand. 
 Most participants also work on quilts using their own sewing machine at ho
 me. Quilts are completed both as individual projects and as group collabor
 ations.\nNew members are welcome\, and will have access to the instruction
 s\, fabrics\, needle and thread required to contribute on-site to the curr
 ent group project.\nRegarding dates: The quilters will not meet when schoo
 l is out. E.g. March break and during the summer (July and August) and dur
 ing December break.
LOCATION:Jones
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3e8cc6414ef43d00981bde
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
