BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tea & Entertainment
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260731T160000
UID:69e1496abd5c392c7644b15f@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy watching DVDs in the Library Auditorium.\nCoffee\, tea a
 nd cookies or snacks will be served after the film. Ingredient lists will 
 be available upon request.\nGrasslands\nGrasslands cover a quarter of the 
 Earth and are home to massive wildlife populations that survive some of th
 e planet’s harshest seasonal extremes. From deadly battles between the f
 ormidable animals and their prey to long-distance migrations and clever an
 imal partnerships\, species across the globe have evolved remarkable ways 
 to endure life on the open plains. Closed captions. 60 minutes.2017.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e1496abd5c392c7644b15f
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
