BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T120000
UID:6a32f17d4407827f8aa59b2b@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a series of 6 classes which have be
 en designed to take a learner with no\, or very few skills\, from zero to 
 a solid grounding in the absolute basics. Each class is set up to connect 
 with the previous and next class in a series format. Registration is requi
 red for the series.\nFriday July 10: Use the Mouse\nFriday July 17: Use th
 e Keyboard\nFriday July 31: Use the Web\nFriday August 7: Use Google Searc
 h and Maps\nFriday August 14: Use Windows\nFriday August 21: Use Email –
  Gmail\nCourse Objective\nUpon completion of this class\, students will be
  able to use a computer mouse and keyboards to navigate the Internet\, Win
 dows\, conduct Google Searches\, and use Gmail.\nPrerequisites: None\nForm
 at: Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Humberwood
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32f17d4407827f8aa59b2b
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 6: Use Gmail
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260729T153000
UID:6a4019fcc7d3cd5800634155@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn to use Gmail\, Google’s free web-based email service.\
 nIn this session you will:\nPractice basic email functions: send\, read\, 
 reply\, forward\, delete email\, and attach files\nReview how spam and jun
 k mail work\nUpon completion of this class students will have a basic unde
 rstanding of how to use email.\nInstructions on how to set up and manage y
 our own free Gmail account are included in the handout.\nPrerequisites: Ba
 sic keyboarding and mouse skills required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstr
 ations
LOCATION:Fairview\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4019fcc7d3cd5800634155
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Trivia Night: All Things Summer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260813T200000
UID:6a4d0172c52cdc3600ef5724@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Test your knowledge playing themed trivia! This month's theme
  is\nAll Things Summer\n. You are welcome to form groups or participate 
 on your own. This program is for adults and seniors and occurs on the sec
 ond Thursday of each month.\nNo registration required. Drop-in until capac
 ity is reached.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Auditorium\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a4d0172c52cdc3600ef5724
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Knit & Crochet
