SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260923T150000
UID:6a31965e7550c8bf9f5dcde6@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a lively and fun discussion about the selected boo
 k.\nSept:\nVioleta\nby Isabel Allende\nOct:\nA Town Called Solace\nby Mary
  Lawson\nNov:\nA Gentleman in Moscow\nby Amor Towles\nDec:\nCreation Lake\
 nby Rachel Cushner\nPlease place a copy of the book on hold\, limited quan
 tities may be made available
LOCATION:Richview\, Room B\, upstairs
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a31965e7550c8bf9f5dcde6
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Finding Recovery Through Exercise Skills and Hope (FRESH): Fridays
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T163000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260821T183000
UID:6931f15d94297d36009e4829@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Drop in\, no registration is required.\nSnacks and refreshments are provid
 ed for all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program
 .\nThis program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S
 .H. initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Browsery
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f15d94297d36009e4829
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
