BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners 1: Use the Mouse
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260719T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260719T153000
UID:6a29de56f56bd86e00b5eb77@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on how to use a mouse for absolute beginners with litt
 le or no computer experience.\nIn this first session you will:\nObserve an
 d practice how to operate a mouse effectively\nUnderstand various mouse po
 inters and cursors\nReview basic keyboard functions\nUse the mouse for bas
 ic Windows functions\nUpon completion of this class students will be able 
 to use a computer mouse at a basic level and will be able to go online for
  additional practice.\nPrerequisites: No computer experience required.\nFo
 rmat: Hands-on with demonstrations\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe pe
 rsonal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Library
  under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The 
 information will only be used for event and program registration\, deliver
 y and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your information
  can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Malvern
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a29de56f56bd86e00b5eb77
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 2: Do More with your Data
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260826T153000
UID:6a512d6c0e562e280098f5cc@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for beginners with li
 ttle or no Excel experience. Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills an
 d learn to use Excel data effectively.\nIn this second session\, you will:
 \nPractice data entry and formatting\nManipulate rows and columns\nCreate 
 and copy simple formulas\nConvert data to a Table then sort and filter\nCr
 eate your first chart\nUpon completion of this class\, you will be able to
  get more from your data using tables\, filters and charts.\nPrerequisites
 : Excel Basics Part 1 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse and keyboard sk
 ills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Learning Center
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a512d6c0e562e280098f5cc
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
