BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Expressions of Wisdom 2.0 Living Stories
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T143000
UID:6a3d7638fddb082f00fdfd28@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Expressions of Wisdom 2.0: Living Stories\nJoin\nLiving Storie
 s\n\, a free and welcoming theatre program where older adults can connect\
 , create\, and share stories through theatre performance.\nParticipants wi
 ll explore storytelling and memory-sharing exercises\, gentle movement\, a
 cting\, playwriting\, and prop-making while building confidence\, and comm
 unity connections. The program will culminate in a community performance c
 elebrating the stories and experiences of the group.\nPresented in collabo
 ration with Arts Etobicoke.\nRegister online or please call the Northern E
 lms branch at 416-394-5230.
LOCATION:Northern Elms
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d7638fddb082f00fdfd28
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Marvel & DC Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260817T200000
UID:69e151ba4dacf581ff8942ad@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Whether you are an avid Marvel and/or DC fan\, or have never r
 ead a comic before but would like to\, join our Marvel/DC book club where 
 we will read a wide variety of graphic novels about these amazing heroes!\
 nMay 4th:\nBatman\n: The Knight by Chip Zdarsky and Carmine Di Giandomeni
 co\nJune 1st:\nDC Pride 2021\nby various writers and artists (also availa
 ble in ebook)\nJuly 6th:\nSpider-Man\n: Life Story by Chip Zdarsky and Mar
 k Bagley (also available in ebook)\nAugust 17th:\nThor: God of Thunder\n: 
 The God Butcher and\nThor : God of Thunder\n: Godbomb by Jason Aaron and 
 Esad Ribic (also available in ebook\; can also be read in one ebook volum
 e as\nThor: The Saga of Gorr the God Butcher\n)\nParticipants are expected
  to pick up the respective books themselves.
LOCATION:Lillian H. Smith\, Basement room A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e151ba4dacf581ff8942ad
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
