BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Be Ready\, Toronto! Emergency Preparedness Workshop for Individual
 s and Households
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T110000
UID:6a2073f443b41b3d006b74a7@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Please note that Hillcrest Library will be closed for renovati
 ons beginning\nMonday\, July 27\, 2026\n\, for approximately four months. 
 The renovation will include essential roof repairs and improvements to the
  accessibility of the library grounds. During this time\, the location of 
 this program may change. Please check back for updates and the latest prog
 ram location information.\nEmergencies can happen anywhere at any time. In
  Canada\, we face numerous hazards\, including wildfires\, flooding\, heat
 waves\, and earthquakes. The Be Ready workshop aims to raise individual an
 d household emergency preparedness.\nIn this free workshop facilitated by 
 the\nToronto Emergency Management Division of the City of Toronto\n\, in p
 artnership with the\nCanadian Red Cross\n\, participants will learn about:
 \nThe potential hazards and risks in their area\nHow to create an emergenc
 y plan\nHow to assemble an emergency kit\nThe importance of social and sup
 port networks during emergencies\nFree program. Register for a reminder. F
 or more information\, please contact the branch.\nInformation Collection N
 otice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto 
