BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Diaries of Mark Robinson\, Algonquin Park Ranger – 1908-1936
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260716T200000
UID:6a1995880c0f2c4503fba568@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Historian Gregory Klages presents\nAlgonquin Diaries\n(Dinerva
 \, 2025 & 2026)\, compiling the diary entries of Mark Robinson about life 
 in Algonquin Park in the early 20th century. Over three decades\, Robinson
  served as a Ranger\, Acting Park Superintendent\, and officer in the Cana
 dian Expeditionary Force. Throughout\, he maintained daily diaries in whic
 h he recorded his experiences of significant social\, political\, cultural
 \, and environmental events.\nThis is an in-person program\, no registrati
 on required.\nAlgonquin Diaries\nAlgonquin Diaries
LOCATION:Brentwood\, Community Room\, Ground Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a1995880c0f2c4503fba568
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
