BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Resilience Reads: a climate neighbourhood reading party
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T183000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T200000
UID:69dd3dd5c1cf6f9a758518cf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us to share the joy of reading\, while building climate r
 esilience knowledge. Members are invited to discuss a book they are readin
 g\, tell stories\,  and empower each other to explore community-driven sol
 utions. Each party will start with a quiet read and reflect time\, with op
 portunities to join group discussions later on over refreshments.\nAPRIL 1
 5-Learning from trees for Earth Month\nThe Overstory\nby Richard Power\nMA
 Y 20-All women are water defenders\nMemory of Water\nby Emmi Itaranta or y
 our favourite book featuring water!\nJUNE 17– Righting our relationship 
 with land\nEarth Keeper\nby N. Scott Momaday or your favourite book that s
 hares how words are medicine!\nJULY 15– Climate migration or the borders
  between us are not lines that divide us\, but seams that connect us\nGun 
 Island\n/\nThe Hungry Tide\nby Amitav Ghosh or your favourite island setti
 ng summer read!\nCopies are available in the branch to pick up\, while sup
 plies last.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on t
 his form is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libra
 ries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only b
 e used for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Quest
 ions about how the library handles your information can be directed to Ans
 werline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, 
 Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Parkdale\, Auditorium A
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69dd3dd5c1cf6f9a758518cf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners: Use Google Search and Maps
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260724T143000
UID:6a3ad4d2fddb082f00fd7644@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:A class on using Google's filters\, tools\, and Maps for absol
 ute beginners with little computer experience.\nIn this session you will:\
 n- Use Google search tools more effectively to find websites\, images\, an
 d news sites\n- Explore Google Maps to find addresses and get directions f
 or transit and road travel.\nUpon completion of this class students will b
 e able to use more advanced search engine features and use Google Maps at 
 a basic level.\nPrerequisites: basic mouse\, keyboarding and internet skil
 ls\nFormat: Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Don Mills\, Youth Hub at lower level
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3ad4d2fddb082f00fd7644
