BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Seniors' Social: NatureTO - Managing Invasive Plants Around  Your 
 Home!
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T153000
UID:6a32984090cc4e3a790ec129@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Calling all older adults!\nCome join us at Morningside library
  every month\, on the last Tuesday of the month\, for a seniors' social. E
 njoy a variety of topics\, guest speakers\, lively conversation\, & fun ac
 tivities!\nJuly's social is a presentation. Join the City of Toronto Urba
 n Forestry team as they discuss invasive plants commonly found around hom
 es in Toronto! Learn how to identify these species\, understand their impa
 ct\, & how to manage them. You will also get tips on supporting local biod
 iversity through enhancing native habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeow
 ners\, & anyone interested in urban ecology!\nThis program is part of TPL'
 s\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends of Toronto Pu
 blic Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Morningside\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32984090cc4e3a790ec129
