BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Memory and Aging: What's Normal\, What's Not\, and What You Can Do
  About It
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260721T140000
UID:6a32ca0ecaf934360063c21a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us as psychologist Dr. Nicole Anderson discusses the kind
 s of cognitive function changes that are a part of healthy aging\, and pro
 vides examples of normal memory slips\, and not so normal memory slips. Th
 is presentation discusses factors affecting cognition\, including medical 
 factors\, and everyday lifestyle factors\, then provides a number of memor
 y strategies that people can use to make their memory function better.\nTh
 is is a drop in program\, no registration is required.
LOCATION:Albion\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32ca0ecaf934360063c21a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Transforming Garbage: Collage a Postcard
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260818T193000
UID:6a35b7e472ddb7360081d5fe@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Gain an understanding of creating art with upcycled materials
  through the art of collage. By using magazines and a card stock surface
 \, participants will start cutting out images and words that relate to the
 ir desired work of art. This workshop will encourage the process of workin
 g with collage as a non-precious material and inspire participants to cr
 eate a piece of art with the materials in their own home/community.\nThis 
 workshop will be delivered by Alysha Rocca\, an emerging artist who holds
  a BFA from OCAD University. Working with the theme of sustainability\, A
 lysha weaves together the threads of feminism and environmental conscious
 ness.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this fo
 rm is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries A
 ct\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used
  for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions a
 bout how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerlin
 e staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toront
 o ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Woodside Square
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a35b7e472ddb7360081d5fe
