BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO: Managing Invasive Plants Around Your Home
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260819T193000
UID:6a0762a143b41b3d0066bfaf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join City of Toronto Urban Forestry staff for a presentation o
 n invasive plants commonly found around homes in Toronto. Learn how to ide
 ntify these species\, understand their impact\, and how to manage them. Yo
 u’ll also get tips on supporting local biodiversity through enhancing na
 tive habitats. Perfect for gardeners\, homeowners\, and anyone interested 
 in urban ecology.\nThe last half hour will be to answer questions and have
  a group discussion.\nDrop-in\, no registration required\nThis program is 
 part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram series\, supported by Friends o
 f Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Eglinton Square\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a0762a143b41b3d0066bfaf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
