UID:6931f2a276261f28005d7d60@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:This program helps people stay active\, make friends\, learn n
 ew skills\, and have fun. Meet new folks\, build connections\, and tell us
  about programs and services you would like to see in the neighbourhood!\n
 Come and join the F.R.E.S.H. group for a Saturday screening of popular mov
 ies.\nWe'll be playing the following films\nAugust 1st –\nNetwork\nAugus
 t 8th –\nThe Rainmaker (1997)\nAugust 15th –\nRoad to Perdition\nAugus
 t 22nd –\nMy Cousin Vinny\nAugust 29th –\nOf Mice and Men (1939)\nDrop
  in\, no registration is required.\nSnacks and refreshments are provided f
 or all participants. Ingredient lists will be available at the program.\nT
 his program is in collaboration with\nGerstein Crisis Centre's F.R.E.S.H. 
 initiative\n.
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, First floor\, Activity Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6931f2a276261f28005d7d60
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Computers for Beginners Series
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260812T153000
UID:6a301aefc7d3cd5800607c04@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Computers for Beginners is a series of 6 classes which have be
 en designed to take a learner with no\, or very few skills\, from zero to 
 a solid grounding in the absolute basics. Each class is set up to connect 
 with the previous and next class in a series format.\nDrop-in. No Registra
 tion is required.\nJuly 15\, Class 1: Use the Mouse\nJuly 22\, Class 2: Us
 e the Keyboard\nJuly 29\, Class 3: Use the Web\nAugust 5\, Class 4: Use Go
 ogle Search and Maps\nAugust 12\, Class 5: Use Windows\nAugust 19\, Class 
 6: Use Email - Gmail
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Learning Centre 2
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a301aefc7d3cd5800607c04
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Card Game Trade & Play
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T150000
UID:6a18dab043b41b3d006a0119@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Bring your Pokemon\, Magic the Gathering or other trading card
  game decks and find other players to challenge and exchange cards with. 
 Drop in\, no registration required.\nThis program is for adult participant
 s only.\nParticipants must bring their own specialized trading card decks 
 and are responsible for any trades that take place during the program.\nUN
 O game cards and standard playing card decks will be made available for pl
 ay.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 2/3\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a18dab043b41b3d006a0119
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260730T200000
UID:694b336b4be11d3d00d9a550@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to the Bloor Gladstone Book Club where we discuss boo
 ks in a fun and friendly atmosphere. New members are most welcome! A limit
 ed number of copies are available for pick up at the first floor desk.\nOu
 r titles for 2026 are:\nJanuary:\nOur Homesick Songs\nby Emma Hooper\nFebr
 uary:\nWillie: The Game Changing Story of the NHL's First Black Player\n
 by Willie O’Ree\nMarch:\nFoster\nby Claire Keegan\nApril:\nCrow Lake\nby
  Mary Lawson\nMay:\nThe Headmasters Wager\nby Vincent Lam\nJune:\nKukum\nb
 y Michel Jean (transl.)\nJuly:\nYellowface\nby R. F. Kuang\nAugust:\nStat
 ion Eleven\nby Emily St. John Mandel\nSeptember:\nRecitatif\n: a story by 
 Toni Morrison\nOctober:\nThe Wife's Tale\nby Aida Edemariam\nNovember:\nRu
 n Towards the Danger: Confrontations With a Body of Memory\nby Sarah Poll
 ey
LOCATION:Bloor/Gladstone\, Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/694b336b4be11d3d00d9a550
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Brain Health
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T143000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260924T153000
UID:69ecdf054dacf581ff8b1661@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:In partnership with Alzheimer Society of Toronto for World Alz
 heimer's Month\, this workshop will teach participants about the risk fac
 tors associated with Alzheimer's disease and dementia and strategies to im
 prove or maintain the health of the brain.\nPlease register with your phon
 e number if you want to be reminded with a phone call. One registration pe
 r person. Do not register twice\, contact staff to confirm if needed.\nThe
  personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Public Libr
 ary under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). T
 he information will only be used for event and program registration\, deli
 very and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your informat
 ion can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-397-598
 1\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ecdf054dacf581ff8b1661
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Investing Basics
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260915T193000
UID:69ecde80b1165a41a66198a2@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:New to investing? Learn the basics of this important part of f
 inancial literacy\, including how to save with the goal of investing\, typ
 es of investments\, how to open an account\, types of accounts\, how to av
 oid financial fraud and scams\, and more.\nPresented by Canadian Investmen
 t Regulatory Organization (CIRO)\, a national self-regulatory organization
  that oversees all investment dealers\, mutual fund dealers and trading ac
 tivity on Canada’s debt and equity marketplaces\nPlease register with yo
 ur phone number if you want to be reminded with a phone call. One registra
 tion per person. Do not register twice\, contact staff to confirm if neede
 d.\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toronto Publ
 ic Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 2
 0(d). The information will only be used for event and program registration
 \, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles your i
 nformation can be directed to Answerline staff at answerline@tpl.ca\, 416-
 397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:Bridlewood\, Auditorium
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69ecde80b1165a41a66198a2
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
