BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:NatureTO:  Our Urban Forest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260918T143000
UID:699f08cc5506be0745fef172@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Toronto has one of the largest urban forests in the world. Joi
 n the\nCity of Toronto Urban Forestry\nteam\nfor an in-library presentatio
 n on this amazing natural habitat that reaches all corners of Toronto.\nWe
 ’ll talk about what makes the urban forest so special and share tools to
  explore and understand it better. Bring questions and curiosities and lea
 ve with emboldened confidence and understanding of your City and the natur
 al world that surrounds you!\nThis is a drop-in program\, no registration 
 required.\nThis program is part of TPL's\nOur Fragile Planet\nprogram seri
 es\, supported by Friends of Toronto Public Library\, South Chapter.​
LOCATION:Woodside Square
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699f08cc5506be0745fef172
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence?
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260728T153000
UID:6a020c6c703c33630026d9fa@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Artificial Intelligence (AI) technologies have become increasi
 ngly prevalent in many aspects of modern life\, including healthcare\, fin
 ance\, transportation\, and entertainment.  Some examples of AI applicati
 ons include virtual assistants like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, f
 raud detection systems\, and personalized recommendations in online shoppi
 ng.\nJoin this beginner in-person class to learn what AI is\, how it learn
 s and predicts outcomes\, considerations when using GenAI applications\, a
 nd how the Internet of Things (IOT) applies to AI.\nInformation Collection
  Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is collected by the Toront
 o Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\,
  and 20(d). The information will only be used for event and program regist
 ration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how the library handles 
 your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca
 \n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G8\nAccessibility\n
 Live or automated closed captioning\, sign language interpretation\, inter
 venor services\, or attendant services are available upon request. Please 
 submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to:\ntpl.ca/accessibility-
 events\n.
LOCATION:S. Walter Stewart\, Learning Centre
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a020c6c703c33630026d9fa
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Signatures
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260831T153000
UID:6a512796fb418a28009a0814@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Learn the basics of creating and requesting digital signatures
  in Adobe Acrobat. In this class you will:\n- Learn what a digital signatu
 re means and basic terminology\n- Learn how to create a signature in Adobe
  Acrobat\, and how to request an e-Signature.\nPrerequisites: Mouse and ke
 yboarding skills required.\nPlease register at tpl.ca or by calling 416-39
 6-8943.
LOCATION:Agincourt\, Learning Centre (LC)\, 1st floor.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a512796fb418a28009a0814
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
