BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Digital Life Skills: Online  Shopping
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260823T153000
UID:6a36ce102ea730c17ab8506c@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:For people who have basic internet skills\, and want to learn 
 how to shop online with confidence. Whether you need groceries or home app
 liances\, almost anything can be purchased and delivered to your home. We 
 teach you how to find goods and services online\, look for customer review
 s or consumer testing results and provide tips and guidelines on how to sh
 op safely\, securely and with confidence. Resource handout provided.\nInfo
 rmation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this form is colle
 cted by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Act\, sectio
 ns 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used for event 
 and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions about how th
 e library handles your information can be directed to Answerline staff at\
 nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto ON M4W 2G
 8.
LOCATION:Albert Campbell\, Learning Centre\, 2nd floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a36ce102ea730c17ab8506c
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Queer Literature Book Club
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260925T200000
UID:6a107f69fab4ff0f649aeb5a@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Welcome to Queer Literature Book Club\, where we're gathering 
 like-minded individuals to gush and gossip about 2SLBTQ+ Literature.\nJoin
  us on Friday evenings once a month for a warm and lively discussion of o
 ur selected books! All adults are welcome!\nIf you're looking to socializ
 e with your local book worms\, this is the group for you!\nThis year we wi
 ll be reading:\nJune -\nFirst meeting - Introductions\, and pick up a cop
 y of\nOpen\, Heaven\nby Sean Hewitt.\nJuly\n-\nOpen\, Heaven\nby Sean Hewi
 tt\nAugust\n-\nI Leave It Up To You\,\nby Jinwoo Chong\nSeptember\n-\nYour
  Driver is Waiting\n\, by Priya Guns\nOctober\n-\nHijab Butch Blues\,\nby 
 Lamya H\nNovember -\nShuggie Bain\,\nby Douglas Stuart\nDecember\n-\nGiova
 nni's Room\,\nby James Baldwin\nBooks will be distributed at each meeting 
 (While supplies last).\nA Library card will be required to check them out.
 \n(These titles are subject to change)
LOCATION:Toronto Reference Library\, Third Floor\, Discussion Room.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a107f69fab4ff0f649aeb5a
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
