BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:What is Artificial Intelligence? - Part 1
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260815T104500
UID:6a3d74f0fddb082f00fdfc1d@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:AI technologies have become increasingly prevalent in many asp
 ects of modern life\, including healthcare\, finance\, transportation\, an
 d entertainment. Some examples of AI applications include virtual assistan
 ts like Siri and Alexa\, self-driving cars\, fraud detection systems\, and
  personalized recommendations in online shopping. Come join this beginner 
 in-person class to learn what AI is\, how to spot when it is being used\, 
 and considerations when using AI.\nWhat is Artificial Intelligence? Part 1
  - August 15\nWhat is Artificial Intelligence? Part 2 - August 22
LOCATION:Parliament Street\, Second Floor Program Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a3d74f0fddb082f00fdfc1d
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
