BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bone Health 101
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260711T153000
UID:6a32b6d690cc4e3a790ec919@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:At least 1 in 3 w​​omen and 1 in 5 men will suffer from a 
 fragility fracture in their lifetime. Join us for an information session 
 with a volunteer facilitator from Osteoporosis Canada and learn how to imp
 rove your bone health\, reduce your risk of osteoporosis and related fract
 ures.\nThe session will cover the following:\nWhat you need to know about 
 bone health and osteoporosis\nThe risk of fracturing a bone\nHow to mainta
 in healthy bones\nImpact of nutrition & physical activity\nFall prevention
 \nRegistration is encouraged.\nDrop-ins are welcome until capacity is reac
 hed.\nInformation Collection Notice:\nThe personal information on this for
 m is collected by the Toronto Public Library under the Public Libraries Ac
 t\, sections 20(a)\, 20(c)\, and 20(d). The information will only be used 
 for event and program registration\, delivery and evaluation. Questions ab
 out how the library handles your information can be directed to Answerline
  staff at\nanswerline@tpl.ca\n\, 416-397-5981\, 789 Yonge Street\, Toronto
  ON M4W 2G8.
LOCATION:North York Central Library\, Room 101\, ground floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a32b6d690cc4e3a790ec919
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 3: PivotTables & Conditional Formatting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261003T113000
UID:6a39833df56bd86e00b860e3@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Build on your basic Microsoft Excel skills and learn to use Ex
 cel data effectively.\nIn this third session\, you will:\nUse Conditional 
 Formatting to visualize data\nExplore the power of PivotTables for data su
 mmary and analysis\nSort and filter the data in tables and using slicers\n
 Take home practice data to improve your new skills\nUpon completion of thi
 s class\, you will be able to get more from your data using Pivot tables.\
 nPrerequisites:  Excel Basics 1 and 2 or equivalent knowledge. Basic mouse
  and keyboard skills required.\nFormat:  Hands-on with demonstrations
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a39833df56bd86e00b860e3
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Excel Basics 1: Create a Simple Spreadsheet
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T110000
UID:6a397ceb4407827f8aa6a244@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:An introductory class on Microsoft Excel for absolute beginner
 s with little or no Excel experience.\nIn this first session\, you will:\n
 Learn the basic function and design of Excel files\nPractice basic data en
 try for text\, numbers\, and basic functions: Sum\, AutoSum and Average\nC
 reate and save your first workbook and worksheets\nUpon completion of this
  class\, you will be able to use Excel at a basic level.\nPrerequisites: B
 asic mouse and keyboard skills are required.\nFormat: Hands-on with demons
 trations
LOCATION:Maryvale\, Meeting Room
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a397ceb4407827f8aa6a244
